eButton`) — give icon-only buttons an `aria-label`, and the content stays in the DOM and accessible since nothing is hidden."},"810":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-drawer-32","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-drawer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/inline-drawer#best-practices","content":"Accordion → `Button slot=\"trigger\"` + `InlineDrawerPanel`. Sidebar rail → controlled state + always-visible children."},"811":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-drawer-33","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-drawer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/inline-drawer#best-practices","content":"For the rail, use numeric (px) `minSize`/`maxSize` so the width animates; `min-content`/`max-content` fit the content exactly but won't animate."},"812":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-drawer-34","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-drawer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/inline-drawer#best-practices","content":"`placement` does not flip in RTL; the side is decided by document/flex order."},"813":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-drawer-35","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-drawer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/inline-drawer#best-practices","content":"Don't nest InlineDrawers."},"814":{"id":"/docs/components/label","page_id":"/docs/components/label","type":"page","content":"Label","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/label"},"815":{"id":"/docs/components/label-0","page_id":"/docs/components/label","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/label","content":"Names a form field. The required asterisk appears when the field is required."},"816":{"id":"/docs/components/label-1","page_id":"/docs/components/label","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/label#features","content":"Features"},"817":{"id":"/docs/components/label-2","page_id":"/docs/components/label","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/label#installation","content":"Installation"},"818":{"id":"/docs/components/label-3","page_id":"/docs/components/label","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/label#examples","content":"Examples"},"819":{"id":"/docs/components/label-4","page_id":"/docs/components/label","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/label#default","content":"Default"},"820":{"id":"/docs/components/label-5","page_id":"/docs/components/label","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/label#props","content":"Props"},"821":{"id":"/docs/components/label-6","page_id":"/docs/components/label","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/label#label","content":"Label"},"822":{"id":"/docs/components/label-7","page_id":"/docs/components/label","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/label#features","content":"Associates the visible name with the field control."},"823":{"id":"/docs/components/label-8","page_id":"/docs/components/label","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/label#features","content":"Applies the label treatment, medium weight, at the surrounding\n`SizeProvider` tier. `size` and `emphasis` work as on `Text`."},"824":{"id":"/docs/components/label-9","page_id":"/docs/components/label","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/label#features","content":"Field CSS adds the required asterisk when the field root is `isRequired`. That is not a Label prop."},"825":{"id":"/docs/components/label-10","page_id":"/docs/components/label","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/label#default","content":"Label names a field. The required asterisk comes from Field CSS when the root is `isRequired`."},"826":{"id":"/docs/components/listbox","page_id":"/docs/components/listbox","type":"page","content":"ListBox","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/listbox"},"827":{"id":"/docs/components/listbox-0","page_id":"/docs/components/listbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/listbox","content":"ListBox is a selectable collection of items rendered inline. Use it for non-popover pickers, inline lists, or as a building block for higher-level components like Select."},"828":{"id":"/docs/components/listbox-1","page_id":"/docs/components/listbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/listbox#features","content":"Features"},"829":{"id":"/docs/components/listbox-2","page_id":"/docs/components/listbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/listbox#installation","content":"Installation"},"830":{"id":"/docs/components/listbox-3","page_id":"/docs/components/listbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/listbox#examples","content":"Examples"},"831":{"id":"/docs/components/listbox-4","page_id":"/docs/components/listbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/listbox#default","content":"Default"},"832":{"id":"/docs/components/listbox-5","page_id":"/docs/components/listbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/listbox#list-box-controlled","content":"List Box Controlled"},"833":{"id":"/docs/components/listbox-6","page_id":"/docs/components/listbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/listbox#list-box-multiple","content":"List Box Multiple"},"834":{"id":"/docs/components/listbox-7","page_id":"/docs/components/listbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/listbox#props","content":"Props"},"835":{"id":"/docs/components/listbox-8","page_id":"/docs/components/listbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/listbox#listbox","content":"ListBox"},"836":{"id":"/docs/components/listbox-9","page_id":"/docs/components/listbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/listbox#listboxitem","content":"ListBoxItem"},"837":{"id":"/docs/components/listbox-10","page_id":"/docs/components/listbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/listbox#features","content":"**Single or multiple selection**: Set `selectionMode=\"single\"` or `\"multiple\"`."},"838":{"id":"/docs/components/listbox-11","page_id":"/docs/components/listbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/listbox#features","content":"**Controlled or uncontrolled**: Use `selectedKeys` and `onSelectionChange` for controlled state, or `defaultSelectedKeys` for uncontrolled."},"839":{"id":"/docs/components/listbox-12","page_id":"/docs/components/listbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/listbox#features","content":"**Layout primitive**: `ListBox` and `ListBoxItem` accept layout props (`gap`, `padding`, etc.) — they extend `FlexOwnProps`."},"840":{"id":"/docs/components/listbox-13","page_id":"/docs/components/listbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/listbox#features","content":"**Composes into other components**: `Select` uses `ListBox` internally; reach for `ListBox` directly when you need an inline list rather than a popover dropdown."},"841":{"id":"/docs/components/listbox-14","page_id":"/docs/components/listbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/listbox#features","content":"**React Aria integration**: Built on React Aria ListBox for accessibility, keyboard navigation, and typeahead."},"842":{"id":"/docs/components/listbox-15","page_id":"/docs/components/listbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/listbox#features","content":"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."},"843":{"id":"/docs/components/listbox-16","page_id":"/docs/components/listbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/listbox#default","content":"Single selection with static children. Use `aria-label` to give the listbox an accessible name."},"844":{"id":"/docs/components/listbox-17","page_id":"/docs/components/listbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/listbox#list-box-controlled","content":"Use `selectedKeys` and `onSelectionChange` for controlled state."},"845":{"id":"/docs/components/listbox-18","page_id":"/docs/components/listbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/listbox#list-box-multiple","content":"Set `selectionMode=\"multiple\"` to allow multiple values. `selectedKeys` is a `Set<Key>` (or the literal `'all'`)."},"846":{"id":"/docs/components/menu","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"page","content":"Menu","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu"},"847":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-0","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu","content":"Accessible dropdown menu with grouping, multi-select checkbox items, leading icons, and submenus."},"848":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-1","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#features","content":"Features"},"849":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-2","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#installation","content":"Installation"},"850":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-3","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#examples","content":"Examples"},"851":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-4","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#default","content":"Default"},"852":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-5","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"853":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-6","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#bottom-sheet","content":"Bottom Sheet"},"854":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-7","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#groups","content":"Groups"},"855":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-8","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#multiple-selection","content":"Multiple Selection"},"856":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-9","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#rich-content-from-an-item","content":"Rich Content From an Item"},"857":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-10","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#single-selection","content":"Single Selection"},"858":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-11","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"859":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-12","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#submenu","content":"Submenu"},"860":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-13","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"861":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-14","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"862":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-15","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#props","content":"Props"},"863":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-16","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#menu","content":"Menu"},"864":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-17","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#menutrigger","content":"MenuTrigger"},"865":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-18","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#menugroup","content":"MenuGroup"},"866":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-19","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#menuitem","content":"MenuItem"},"867":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-20","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#menuseparator","content":"MenuSeparator"},"868":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-21","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#submenutrigger","content":"SubmenuTrigger"},"869":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-22","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu","content":"An accessible dropdown menu built on React Aria. It supports grouping with optional\ntitles, multi-select checkbox items, leading icons, submenus, and two sizes. It\nreuses Antares' `Popover` for the overlay and `Checkbox` indicator for selection."},"870":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-23","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#features","content":"Grouping with an optional title via `MenuGroup`, plus `MenuSeparator` dividers"},"871":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-24","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#features","content":"Multi-select groups: set `selectionMode=\"multiple\"` on a `MenuGroup` to render\nits items as checkboxes, while other groups stay plain action items"},"872":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-25","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#features","content":"Optional leading `icon` per item; links (`href`) and disabled items"},"873":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-26","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#features","content":"Submenus via `SubmenuTrigger`"},"874":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-27","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#features","content":"Two sizes (`sm`, `md`); set `size` explicitly on each submenu `Menu`"},"875":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-28","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#features","content":"Usable anchored to a trigger or standalone (e.g. inside a bottom-sheet `Drawer`)"},"876":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-29","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#default","content":"A trigger with plain action items."},"877":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-30","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#controlled","content":"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."},"878":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-31","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#bottom-sheet","content":"On small screens a menu often reads better as a bottom sheet than an anchored\npopover. Since `Menu` works standalone, drop it into a bottom `Drawer`."},"879":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-32","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#groups","content":"Labeled groups separated by dividers, a multi-select checkbox group mixed with\nplain action groups, leading icons, a disabled item, and a link."},"880":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-33","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#multiple-selection","content":"A `MenuGroup` with `selectionMode=\"multiple\"` renders its items as checkboxes.\nDrive the checked items with `selectedKeys` + `onSelectionChange` or\nseed them uncontrolled with `defaultSelectedKeys`. Keys correspond to each\n`MenuItem`'s `id`."},"881":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-34","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#rich-content-from-an-item","content":"A `Menu` is a collection, so it only renders `MenuItem`, `MenuGroup`,\n`MenuSeparator`, and `SubmenuTrigger` children. Rich content inside a `Menu`\nor submenu is not supported. To show a `Calendar`, let the item close the\nmenu from `onAction` and open a separate `Popover` anchored to the trigger\nwith `triggerRef`."},"882":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-35","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#single-selection","content":"A `MenuGroup` with `selectionMode=\"single\"` lets one item be selected at a time.\nDrive it with `selectedKeys` + `onSelectionChange` or seed it uncontrolled with\n`defaultSelectedKeys`. Keys correspond to each `MenuItem`'s `id`."},"883":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-36","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#sizes","content":"`size` controls item density. Shown here as two standalone menus so both\nsizes are visible at once; in practice you set `size` on the `Menu` inside a\n`MenuTrigger`."},"884":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-37","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#submenu","content":"Nested menus via `SubmenuTrigger`."},"885":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-38","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#accessibility","content":"**Space/Enter**: activate an item; **Escape**: close"},"886":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-39","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#accessibility","content":"**Arrow Up/Down**: move between items; **Home/End**: first/last"},"887":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-40","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#accessibility","content":"**Arrow Right/Left**: open/close a submenu"},"888":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-41","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#accessibility","content":"**Type to select**: jump to a matching item (string labels are used as `textValue`)"},"889":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-42","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#accessibility","content":"Multi-select items use RAC's `menuitemcheckbox` role; the checkbox indicator is\ndecorative (`aria-hidden`) and the item owns interaction"},"890":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-43","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#best-practices","content":"Give each selectable `MenuItem` a stable `id`, and provide the `Menu` an\n`aria-label` when there is no visible label."},"891":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-44","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#best-practices","content":"Use a leading `icon` for recognition, not as the only label - keep a text label."},"892":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-45","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#best-practices","content":"Reserve checkbox groups for multi-select; use plain groups for one-shot actions."},"893":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-46","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#best-practices","content":"A `Menu` is a collection: it only renders `MenuItem`, `MenuGroup`,\n`MenuSeparator`, and `SubmenuTrigger`. For rich content (a `Calendar`, a form),\nclose the menu from `onAction` and open a separate `Popover` anchored with\n`triggerRef` instead of putting it in a submenu."},"894":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"page","content":"MetricsLockup","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup"},"895":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-0","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","content":"The MetricsLockup component displays a single metric with an optional title, info tooltip, trend indicator, and description."},"896":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-1","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#installation","content":"Installation"},"897":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-2","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#examples","content":"Examples"},"898":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-3","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#default","content":"Default"},"899":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-4","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#with-trend","content":"With Trend"},"900":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-5","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#compact","content":"Compact"},"901":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-6","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"902":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-7","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Keyboard"},"903":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-8","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#aria","content":"ARIA"},"904":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-9","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"905":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-10","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#props","content":"Props"},"906":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-11","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#metricslockup","content":"MetricsLockup"},"907":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-12","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","content":"MetricsLockup displays a metric value prominently, with an optional title and tooltip for context, an optional trend icon to show direction of change, and a description label below the value."},"908":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-13","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#default","content":"A metric with a title, info tooltip, value, and description."},"909":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-14","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#with-trend","content":"Use the `trend` prop to show a directional icon next to the description. Accepts `'positive'`, `'negative'`, or `'neutral'`."},"910":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-15","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#compact","content":"Use the `compact` prop to render the metric value and description inline rather than stacked."},"911":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-16","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Key"},"912":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-17","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Description"},"913":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-18","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Tab"},"914":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-19","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Moves focus to the info trigger button and shows the tooltip"},"915":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-20","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Escape"},"916":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-21","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Closes the tooltip"},"917":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-22","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#aria","content":"The info trigger button uses `aria-label=\"More information\"` to describe its purpose."},"918":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-23","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#aria","content":"The tooltip uses `role=\"tooltip\"` and is associated with the info trigger via `aria-describedby`."},"919":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-24","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#aria","content":"The info trigger has a minimum touch target of 44×44px, achieved via a CSS pseudo-element, to meet WCAG 2.5.5."},"920":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-25","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#best-practices","content":"Keep tooltip content concise and informative."},"921":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-26","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#best-practices","content":"The `data` prop accepts strings or numbers — format currency and percentages before passing them in."},"922":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-27","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#best-practices","content":"`titleInfo` requires `title` to be set — the info icon is contextually tied to the title label. If `title` is absent, `titleInfo` has no effect."},"923":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-28","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#best-practices","content":"`trend` is intended to accompany `description` to provide temporal context (e.g. \"↑ +3% vs. last month\"). A trend icon alone, with no description, leaves the direction unanchored (\"up since *when*?\"). If `description` is not provided, `trend` has no effect."},"924":{"id":"/docs/components/modal","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"page","content":"Modal","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal"},"925":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-0","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal","content":"The Modal component presents a dialog window over the page that focuses the user's attention on a single task or piece of information."},"926":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-1","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#installation","content":"Installation"},"927":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-2","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#examples","content":"Examples"},"928":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-3","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#default","content":"Default"},"929":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-4","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"930":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-5","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#scrollable","content":"Scrollable"},"931":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-6","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#triggerless","content":"Triggerless"},"932":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-7","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#size","content":"Size"},"933":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-8","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#with-text-lockup","content":"With Text Lockup"},"934":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-9","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"935":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-10","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#keyboard-interaction","content":"Keyboard interaction"},"936":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-11","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#aria","content":"ARIA"},"937":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-12","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"938":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-13","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#props","content":"Props"},"939":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-14","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#modal","content":"Modal"},"940":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-15","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#modaltrigger","content":"ModalTrigger"},"941":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-16","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal","content":"`ModalTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Modal>`, handling open state automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."},"942":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-17","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal","content":"The modal is a `SizeProvider`. It opens at the size of the scope around its trigger, even though it renders in a portal, and `size` overrides that."},"943":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-18","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#default","content":"Compose a Modal from a `Heading slot=\"title\"`, a `CloseButton`, `Content`, and a\n`ButtonGroup`. `ModalTrigger` opens the Modal and manages its open/close state."},"944":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-19","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#controlled","content":"Pass `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` to `ModalTrigger` to control the open state externally."},"945":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-20","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#scrollable","content":"When the content is taller than the viewport, the `Content` region scrolls while the title\nrow and the `ButtonGroup` stay pinned."},"946":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-21","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#triggerless","content":"`Modal` accepts `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` directly, so it can be controlled without a\n`ModalTrigger`. Useful when the modal is opened from several places at once."},"947":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-22","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#size","content":"`size` sets the modal's text, controls, and spacing. Without it, the modal follows the size\nscope around its trigger."},"948":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-23","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#with-text-lockup","content":"A `TextLockup` in the content keeps its own title. The modal's `Heading slot=\"title\"` still names\nthe dialog."},"949":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-24","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#keyboard-interaction","content":"Key"},"950":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-25","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#keyboard-interaction","content":"Action"},"951":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-26","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#keyboard-interaction","content":"`Tab`"},"952":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-27","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#keyboard-interaction","content":"Moves focus to the next focusable element inside the modal"},"953":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-28","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#keyboard-interaction","content":"`Escape`"},"954":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-29","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#keyboard-interaction","content":"Closes the modal (unless `isKeyboardDismissDisabled`)"},"955":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-30","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#aria","content":"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"},"956":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-31","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#aria","content":"Focus is trapped within the modal while open and returned to the trigger on close"},"957":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-32","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#best-practices","content":"Always include a `Heading slot=\"title\"` so the dialog has an accessible name; otherwise pass `aria-label`/`aria-labelledby` on `<Modal>`"},"958":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-33","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#best-practices","content":"Pair every action button with `slot=\"close\"` when it should dismiss the modal"},"959":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-34","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#best-practices","content":"Set `isDismissable={false}` to prevent outside-click dismissal for required confirmations; to also block `Escape`, pass `isKeyboardDismissDisabled`"},"960":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"page","content":"NumberField","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field"},"961":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-0","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field","content":"NumberField is a composed numeric input with min/max/step and optional increment/decrement stepper buttons. Use it in forms for quantities, amounts, or percentages."},"962":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-1","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#features","content":"Features"},"963":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-2","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#installation","content":"Installation"},"964":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-3","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#examples","content":"Examples"},"965":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-4","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#default","content":"Default"},"966":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-5","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"967":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-6","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#invalid","content":"Invalid"},"968":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-7","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"969":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-8","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#hide-stepper","content":"Hide Stepper"},"970":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-9","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#value-scale","content":"Value Scale"},"971":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-10","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#format-options-numbering-system","content":"Format options (numbering system)"},"972":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-11","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"973":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-12","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#text-steppers","content":"Text Steppers"},"974":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-13","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#props","content":"Props"},"975":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-14","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#numberfield","content":"NumberField"},"976":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-15","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#features","content":"**Composable interior**: Compose `Label`, the control, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. Nothing is added for you, and what you write keeps the order you wrote it in"},"977":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-16","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#features","content":"**Steppers**: A stepper is a `Group` holding `Button slot=\"decrement\"`, an `Input`, and `Button slot=\"increment\"`. Left empty, each button takes its icon and `variant=\"control\"` from the field, so no icon imports are needed. Compose a bare `Input` instead for a plain numeric input"},"978":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-17","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#features","content":"**Sizes**: The field is a `SizeProvider`. `size` (`sm`, `md`, `lg`) sets its label, input, steppers, description, and error; without it, the field follows the surrounding scope"},"979":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-18","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#features","content":"**Value scale**: `minValue`, `maxValue`, `step`, and `formatOptions` configure the numeric behavior"},"980":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-19","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#features","content":"**Controlled or uncontrolled**: Use `value` and `onChange` for controlled state, or `defaultValue` for uncontrolled"},"981":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-20","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#features","content":"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"},"982":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-21","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#default","content":"Minimal usage with a `Label`, min/max, and stepper `Button`s."},"983":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-22","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#controlled","content":"Use `value` and `onChange` for controlled state."},"984":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-23","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#invalid","content":"Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` for validation feedback."},"985":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-24","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#disabled","content":"Use `isDisabled` to prevent input."},"986":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-25","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#hide-stepper","content":"Compose without stepper `Button`s for a plain numeric input."},"987":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-26","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#value-scale","content":"Use `minValue`, `maxValue`, and `step` to set the allowed values. Steps are calculated from the minimum value."},"988":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-27","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#format-options-numbering-system","content":"By default, NumberField displays the value using the numbering system for the user's locale. Use the `formatOptions` prop to override the numbering system by setting the Unicode numbering system locale extension."},"989":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-28","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#sizes","content":"`size` sets the label, input, and steppers. Without it, the field follows the surrounding size\nscope."},"990":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-29","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#text-steppers","content":"Compose with `children` to replace the stepper icons with your own content, such as text."},"991":{"id":"/docs/components/popover","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"page","content":"Popover","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover"},"992":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-0","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover","content":"The Popover component is an overlay element positioned relative to a trigger element."},"993":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-1","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#installation","content":"Installation"},"994":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-2","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#examples","content":"Examples"},"995":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-3","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#default","content":"Default"},"996":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-4","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#custom-anchor","content":"Custom Anchor"},"997":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-5","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#title-and-close-button","content":"Title and Close Button"},"998":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-6","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"999":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-7","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#keyboard","content":"Keyboard"},"1000":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-8","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#aria","content":"ARIA"},"1001":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-9","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"1002":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-10","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#props","content":"Props"},"1003":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-11","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#popover","content":"Popover"},"1004":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-12","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#popovertrigger","content":"PopoverTrigger"},"1005":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-13","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover","content":"`PopoverTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Popover>`, handling open state and positioning automatically.\nBased on RAC `DialogTrigger`. To anchor a popover to an element it doesn't wrap, pass `triggerRef` instead."},"1006":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-14","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#default","content":"Use it with `<PopoverTrigger>`, which wraps both the popover content and an interactive trigger element (for example, a `Button`)."},"1007":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-15","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#custom-anchor","content":"To position a popover relative to a different element than its trigger, use the `triggerRef` and `isOpen` props instead of `<PopoverTrigger>`. `onOpenChange` is called when the user opens or closes the popover."},"1008":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-16","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#title-and-close-button","content":"Add a `Heading slot=\"title\"` and a `CloseButton` for a titled, dismissible popover. The heading\nalso gives the dialog its accessible name."},"1009":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-17","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#keyboard","content":"Key"},"1010":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-18","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#keyboard","content":"Action"},"1011":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-19","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#keyboard","content":"`Enter/Space`"},"1012":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-20","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#keyboard","content":"Opens the popover from its trigger"},"1013":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-21","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#keyboard","content":"`Escape`"},"1014":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-22","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#keyboard","content":"Closes the popover"},"1015":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-23","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#aria","content":"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"},"1016":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-24","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#aria","content":"A `Heading slot=\"title\"` labels the dialog via `aria-labelledby`. Without one, a popover inside\na `PopoverTrigger` falls back to being labelled by its trigger; standing alone with\n`triggerRef` it needs an explicit `aria-label`"},"1017":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-25","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#best-practices","content":"Pass an `aria-label` when anchoring with `triggerRef` instead of wrapping a `PopoverTrigger`,\nsince there is no trigger to borrow the name from."},"1018":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-26","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#best-practices","content":"Popover width is determined by its content, and it's recommended to keep it under 400px."},"1019":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","type":"page","content":"Pagination","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pagination"},"1020":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-0","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination","content":"A pagination component with prev/next buttons and dot indicators, configurable page limits, and optional visibility of controls and dots"},"1021":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-1","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pagination#installation","content":"Installation"},"1022":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-2","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pagination#examples","content":"Examples"},"1023":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-3","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pagination#default","content":"Default"},"1024":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-4","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pagination#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"1025":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-5","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pagination#default-active","content":"Default Active"},"1026":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-6","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pagination#with-limit","content":"With Limit"},"1027":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-7","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pagination#onchange-event","content":"onChange Event"},"1028":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-8","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pagination#props","content":"Props"},"1029":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-9","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pagination#pagination","content":"Pagination"},"1030":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-10","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#default","content":"The default pagination is uncontrolled. It renders prev/next buttons and one dot per page. The `total` prop sets the number of items."},"1031":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-11","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#controlled","content":"Pass `activeIndex` and `onChange` to control the active page externally."},"1032":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-12","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#default-active","content":"Use `defaultActiveIndex` to set the starting page in uncontrolled mode."},"1033":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-13","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#with-limit","content":"Limit the number of items shown per page. When `limit` is greater than 1, the number of pages (dots) is derived from `Math.ceil(total / limit)`. For example, 10 items with a limit of 3 produces 4 pages (dots)."},"1034":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-14","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#onchange-event","content":"The `onChange` callback fires with the new page index whenever the user navigates."},"1035":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"page","content":"Pressable","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable"},"1036":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-0","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable","content":"A wrapperless interaction primitive that adds accessible press behavior to a single child element."},"1037":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-1","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#features","content":"Features"},"1038":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-2","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#installation","content":"Installation"},"1039":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-3","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#examples","content":"Examples"},"1040":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-4","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#default","content":"Default"},"1041":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-5","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#customization","content":"Customization"},"1042":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-6","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"1043":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-7","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"1044":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-8","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"1045":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-9","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#props","content":"Props"},"1046":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-10","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#pressable","content":"Pressable"},"1047":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-11","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#features","content":"Adds accessible press behavior to an existing visual component."},"1048":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-12","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#features","content":"Applies interaction states directly to the child without adding a wrapper element."},"1049":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-13","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#features","content":"Supports pointer, touch, and keyboard interactions through React Aria."},"1050":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-14","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#features","content":"Preserves the child's layout, shape, and base visual styling while adding state feedback."},"1051":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-15","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#default","content":"Add accessible press behavior to an existing visual component without adding a wrapper element.\nThe surface supports pointer, touch, and keyboard activation."},"1052":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-16","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#customization","content":"Use `Pressable` when an existing visual component or layout surface needs press behavior while keeping its own DOM element, layout, and styles. The child must be a single element that forwards its ref and accepts the DOM, ARIA, and event props supplied by React Aria."},"1053":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-17","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#customization","content":"Use `Button` when you need a standard button control with button-specific sizing, layout, and visual variants."},"1054":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-18","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#customization","content":"Pass `onPress` for the action instead of wiring separate pointer and keyboard handlers:"},"1055":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-19","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#accessibility","content":"`Pressable` accepts the React Aria press props, including `onPress`, `onPressStart`, `onPressEnd`, `onPressUp`, and `onPressChange`."},"1056":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-20","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#accessibility","content":"Use a semantic interactive element when possible. For a non-semantic child such as `Avatar` or `Box`, provide an appropriate interactive role and an accessible name. Pressable makes the child focusable when the required props are forwarded."},"1057":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-21","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#accessibility","content":"Do not add `role=\"button\"` to a native `<button>` or `<a>` unless you intentionally need to change its semantics. Use a dedicated semantic component such as `Button`, `LinkButton`, `Menu`, or `ToggleButton` when that control's meaning is known."},"1058":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-22","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#best-practices","content":"Prefer a native interactive element or a semantic Antares component when the interaction meaning is known."},"1059":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-23","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#best-practices","content":"Avoid nesting interactive elements inside the child passed to `Pressable`."},"1060":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-24","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#best-practices","content":"`Pressable` automatically applies React Aria state attributes such as `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`, `[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` to the child. Ensure the child component styles these states appropriately if it overrides the default `Pressable` styles."},"1061":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-25","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#troubleshooting","content":"If React Aria warns that the child must be focusable, ensure it is a single element that forwards its ref, `tabIndex`, DOM props, and ARIA attributes."},"1062":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-26","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#troubleshooting","content":"If `onPress` does not fire, confirm that the child forwards event handlers and is not disabled by another component."},"1063":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","type":"page","content":"ProgressBar","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-bar"},"1064":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-0","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-bar","content":"A progress bar shows determinate or indeterminate progress of an operation over time"},"1065":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-1","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#installation","content":"Installation"},"1066":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-2","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#examples","content":"Examples"},"1067":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-3","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#default","content":"Default"},"1068":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-4","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"1069":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-5","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#statuses","content":"Statuses"},"1070":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-6","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#indeterminate","content":"Indeterminate"},"1071":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-7","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"1072":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-8","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#aria-support","content":"ARIA Support"},"1073":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-9","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#props","content":"Props"},"1074":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-10","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#progressbar","content":"ProgressBar"},"1075":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-11","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#default","content":"A determinate progress bar with a label and helper text."},"1076":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-12","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#sizes","content":"Three track heights are available: `xs` (6px), `sm` (12px), and `md` (24px)."},"1077":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-13","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#statuses","content":"Use the `status` prop to communicate intent: `default`, `success`, `warning`, or `critical`. Pair with `helperText` to provide additional context."},"1078":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-14","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#indeterminate","content":"Use indeterminate progress while preparing an upload whose total size is unknown.\nOnce the total is known, set `isIndeterminate` to false and supply a measured value."},"1079":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-15","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#aria-support","content":"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"},"1080":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-16","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#aria-support","content":"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value"},"1081":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-17","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#aria-support","content":"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"},"1082":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-18","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#aria-support","content":"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`)"},"1083":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-19","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#aria-support","content":"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"},"1084":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"page","content":"ProgressSteps","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps"},"1085":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-0","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps","content":"A multi-step progress indicator for wizard and onboarding flows."},"1086":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-1","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#features","content":"Features"},"1087":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-2","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#installation","content":"Installation"},"1088":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-3","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#examples","content":"Examples"},"1089":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-4","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#default","content":"Default"},"1090":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-5","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#not-started","content":"Not started"},"1091":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-6","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#vertical","content":"Vertical"},"1092":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-7","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#interactive","content":"Interactive"},"1093":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-8","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"1094":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-9","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#hide-step-numbers","content":"Hide Step Numbers"},"1095":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-10","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#customization","content":"Customization"},"1096":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-11","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"1097":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-12","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"1098":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-13","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"1099":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-14","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#props","content":"Props"},"1100":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-15","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#progresssteps","content":"ProgressSteps"},"1101":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-16","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#progressstep","content":"ProgressStep"},"1102":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-17","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#features","content":"Horizontal and vertical orientations"},"1103":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-18","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#features","content":"Four completion statuses (`none`, `partial`, `complete`, `error`) with status icons"},"1104":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-19","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#features","content":"Timeline (past / current / future) derived from a single `currentStep` prop"},"1105":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-20","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#features","content":"Auto-generated step numbers (opt out with `hideStepNumbers`)"},"1106":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-21","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#features","content":"Interactive (navigable) and inert (display-only) steps"},"1107":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-22","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#features","content":"Title truncation and RTL support"},"1108":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-23","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#features","content":"Rendered as a `<nav>` landmark with an ordered list for assistive technology"},"1109":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-24","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#default","content":"A horizontal stepper. `currentStep` marks the active step; earlier steps are `past`, later are `future`. Each `status` sets the step's icon, and an `error` step turns its accent bar red."},"1110":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-25","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#not-started","content":"No `currentStep`: the flow hasn't started, so every step is `future` and none is marked current."},"1111":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-26","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#vertical","content":"Vertical orientation: accent bar on the leading edge, steps stacked in a column."},"1112":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-27","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#interactive","content":"Interactive steps: each `onPress` navigates the wizard by updating `currentStep`."},"1113":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-28","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#disabled","content":"A disabled interactive step is muted, not focusable, and cannot be activated."},"1114":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-29","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#hide-step-numbers","content":"Step numbers are shown by default; `hideStepNumbers` omits the \"N. \" prefix."},"1115":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-30","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#customization","content":"Step numbers (`\"N. \"`) are prepended automatically — keep them where possible, as user testing shows people recognize the component better with them. Set `hideStepNumbers` to omit them."},"1116":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-31","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#customization","content":"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."},"1117":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-32","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#customization","content":"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."},"1118":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-33","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#customization","content":"`status` is independent of timeline and only controls the status icon and (for `error`) the accent bar color."},"1119":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-34","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#customization","content":"Pass `className` to the container or an individual step to extend the styles."},"1120":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-35","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#accessibility","content":"The container renders a `<nav>` landmark; set `aria-label` to name it (defaults to `\"Progress\"`)."},"1121":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-36","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#accessibility","content":"Steps are an ordered list (`<ol>`/`<li>`) so assistive technology conveys position and count."},"1122":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-37","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#accessibility","content":"The current step is marked with `aria-current=\"step\"`."},"1123":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-38","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#accessibility","content":"Interactive steps are real buttons: focusable in the natural **Tab** order and activated with **Enter** or **Space**. Status icons are decorative (`aria-hidden`)."},"1124":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-39","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#accessibility","content":"Focus is shown with a visible outline; disabled steps use `0.4` opacity and are not focusable."},"1125":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-40","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#best-practices","content":"Drive the timeline from `currentStep` rather than styling individual steps."},"1126":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-41","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#best-practices","content":"Provide `onPress` only for steps a user can actually navigate to; leave it off for display-only steps."},"1127":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-42","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#best-practices","content":"Keep titles short — they truncate with an ellipsis when space is tight."},"1128":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-43","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#best-practices","content":"Always give the container an `aria-label` that describes the flow (e.g. `\"Checkout progress\"`)."},"1129":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-44","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#troubleshooting","content":"**No step is highlighted:** `currentStep` is omitted, negative, or out of range. Set it to the active step's 0-based index."},"1130":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-45","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#troubleshooting","content":"**A step isn't clickable:** it has no `onPress`, so it's inert by design. Add `onPress` to make it interactive."},"1131":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-46","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#troubleshooting","content":"**Titles overflow:** that's expected — titles truncate. Shorten the title."},"1132":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"page","content":"RangeField","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field"},"1133":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-0","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field","content":"RangeField lets users select one numeric value or a related set of values on a bounded scale."},"1134":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-1","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Features"},"1135":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-2","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#installation","content":"Installation"},"1136":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-3","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#examples","content":"Examples"},"1137":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-4","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#default","content":"Default"},"1138":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-5","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"1139":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-6","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"1140":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-7","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#labels","content":"Labels"},"1141":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-8","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#value-display","content":"Value Display"},"1142":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-9","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#markers","content":"Markers"},"1143":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-10","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#range","content":"Range"},"1144":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-11","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"1145":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-12","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"Accessible names"},"1146":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-13","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Keyboard interaction"},"1147":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-14","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"1148":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-15","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#props","content":"Props"},"1149":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-16","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#rangefield","content":"RangeField"},"1150":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-17","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"1151":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-18","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#a-thumb-is-missing-a-label-or-form-value","content":"A thumb is missing a label or form value"},"1152":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-19","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#typescript-reports-the-wrong-callback-value-type","content":"TypeScript reports the wrong callback value type"},"1153":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-20","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-controlled-thumbs-do-not-move","content":"The controlled thumbs do not move"},"1154":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-21","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#values-snap-unexpectedly","content":"Values snap unexpectedly"},"1155":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-22","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-final-marker-is-missing","content":"The final marker is missing"},"1156":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-23","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#markers-are-crowded-or-rendering-is-slow","content":"Markers are crowded or rendering is slow"},"1157":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-24","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-value-or-endpoint-labels-are-blank","content":"The value or endpoint labels are blank"},"1158":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-25","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#negative-values-do-not-behave-as-expected","content":"Negative values do not behave as expected"},"1159":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-26","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-range-configuration-is-invalid","content":"The range configuration is invalid"},"1160":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-27","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Select one value or render one thumb for each value in an array"},"1161":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-28","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Supports controlled and uncontrolled values with typed change callbacks"},"1162":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-29","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Provides localized value output, endpoint labels, descriptions, and markers"},"1163":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-30","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Integrates with native forms, keyboard, pointer, and touch interaction through React Aria"},"1164":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-31","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#default","content":"Minimal usage with a single value and min/max bounds."},"1165":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-32","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#controlled","content":"Use `onChange` for immediate updates and `onChangeEnd` for work that should run after interaction finishes."},"1166":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-33","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#disabled","content":"Use `isDisabled` when the value is visible but unavailable for interaction."},"1167":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-34","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#labels","content":"Combine an input label, value label, range labels, and helper text when users need additional context."},"1168":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-35","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#value-display","content":"Use `valueLabel` to show formatted values, static context, or output derived from the current slider state."},"1169":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-36","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#markers","content":"Use `markers` to expose a manageable set of discrete steps for a single value."},"1170":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-37","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#range","content":"Pass a `number[]` to render a range with two thumbs and step markers."},"1171":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-38","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"For a single value, prefer a visible `label`; use `aria-label` only when equivalent visible context already exists."},"1172":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-39","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"For an array, provide one descriptive `thumbLabels` entry for every value. Entries are matched by index, so keep them aligned when values are added, removed, or reordered. Describe each thumb's purpose, such as `Lower warning threshold`, rather than its current number."},"1173":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-40","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"`thumbNames` configures native form field names and does not provide accessible labels. Likewise, `valueLabel`, `minLabel`, and `maxLabel` are visual context rather than substitutes for accessible naming."},"1174":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-41","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Each thumb follows the React Aria slider keyboard model:"},"1175":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-42","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Tab and Shift+Tab move among thumbs and surrounding controls."},"1176":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-43","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Arrow Right and Arrow Up increase the focused value by `step`."},"1177":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-44","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Arrow Left and Arrow Down decrease the focused value by `step`."},"1178":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-45","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Home and End move the focused thumb to its permitted bounds."},"1179":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-46","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Page Up and Page Down make larger changes."},"1180":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-47","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Directional behavior follows the user's locale where appropriate. Pointer, touch, and keyboard interaction all use the same scale and constraints."},"1181":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-48","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Markers are decorative and hidden from the accessibility tree. Ensure the field label, thumb labels, bounds, step, and formatted values communicate all required information without relying on marker appearance."},"1182":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-49","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use an array only when every entry has a clear, independently adjustable meaning."},"1183":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-50","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Keep `value`, `thumbLabels`, and `thumbNames` aligned by index."},"1184":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-51","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use thumb labels that explain purpose instead of repeating the current number."},"1185":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-52","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Keep array values in a stable semantic order. If crossing or reordering thumbs would make their meaning ambiguous, enforce the appropriate ordering in product state."},"1186":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-53","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Avoid large value arrays. Every entry creates another focusable control, which increases keyboard effort and cognitive load."},"1187":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-54","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Set meaningful `minValue`, `maxValue`, and `step` values. The scale should match the precision users actually need."},"1188":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-55","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use markers only when there are few enough steps to scan. Tiny steps across a large range can create an excessive number of DOM elements."},"1189":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-56","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `formatOptions` for currency, percentages, measurements, and other locale-sensitive units so values display and announce their meaning."},"1190":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-57","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `description` for persistent guidance and `isRequired` when a value is required."},"1191":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-58","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `isDisabled` when the value should remain visible but unavailable for interaction."},"1192":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-59","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `onChange` for lightweight immediate feedback and `onChangeEnd` for expensive requests, filtering, or calculations."},"1193":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-60","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use a text-entry control when exact numeric input is essential. A track is best for exploring or adjusting values within known bounds."},"1194":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-61","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#a-thumb-is-missing-a-label-or-form-value","content":"Check the same index in `thumbLabels` and `thumbNames`. Each array entry renders a thumb, and its accessible label and form name are read from the corresponding positions. A form name does not replace an accessible label."},"1195":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-62","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#typescript-reports-the-wrong-callback-value-type","content":"Keep the controlled or default value and callback signatures consistent. When inference is unavailable, provide the generic explicitly: `<RangeField<number>>` for a scalar or `<RangeField<number[]>>` for an array."},"1196":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-63","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-controlled-thumbs-do-not-move","content":"The `value` prop is the source of truth. Update the scalar or array in `onChange` without changing its intended shape. For arrays, return a new array so application state observes the update."},"1197":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-64","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#values-snap-unexpectedly","content":"Verify that `step` represents the intended interval from `minValue`. Every thumb snaps to valid positions on the same configured scale."},"1198":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-65","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-final-marker-is-missing","content":"Markers begin at `minValue` and appear at complete step positions. `maxValue` receives a marker only when the range is evenly divisible by `step`."},"1199":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-66","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#markers-are-crowded-or-rendering-is-slow","content":"Increase `step` or omit `markers`. Large ranges with small steps can produce many decorative elements even when users cannot distinguish them visually."},"1200":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-67","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-value-or-endpoint-labels-are-blank","content":"Enable automatic current-value output with `valueLabel={true}` or provide custom content. `minLabel` and `maxLabel` display only explicitly supplied content; neither defaults to a numeric bound or receives `formatOptions`."},"1201":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-68","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#negative-values-do-not-behave-as-expected","content":"Negative values are supported. Set a negative `minValue` and ensure every scalar or array value remains within the configured bounds."},"1202":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-69","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-range-configuration-is-invalid","content":"Provide finite bounds where `minValue` is less than `maxValue`, a finite `step` greater than zero, and finite values inside the configured range."},"1203":{"id":"/docs/components/radio","page_id":"/docs/components/radio","type":"page","content":"Radio","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/radio"},"1204":{"id":"/docs/components/radio-0","page_id":"/docs/components/radio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radio","content":"A